  "description": "XIXGAQ crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group C 2/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C192 H250 O90 Tb9 1+,N1 O3 1-,x(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Tb1 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb2 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb3 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb4 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb5 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb6 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb7 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb8 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb9 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 20 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.601-5.106 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 88.72-168.93°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Tb9(Sal-PEG-2)16(μ-OH)10](NO3). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 1 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
